  "details": "In particular in certain worlds the push to talk button (V) and radial menu button (R) will just stop responding without any clear cause. This has been tested on two Windows 11 PCs with the same results and has persisted for months.\n\nThere are no clear reproduceable steps that I have found, but it appears to happen much more often in certain worlds, when I have been running around with Shift or when I have been tabbing in and out. However, the bug doesn't trigger immediately in connection with any of these actions making the direct cause a mystery.\n\nTwo notable worlds where it triggers often are:\n\n1. EN-JP Language Exchange\n\n2. Trash Compactor\n\nPressing Escape temporarily clears the bug. I have confirmed it isn't because VRChat loses window focus because other buttons behave like normal when the bug triggers.\n\nPossible duplicate with: https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/push-to-talk-key-v-randomly-stops-working",
